**Rate limiting (new, this task)**
- `backend/src/main/java/com/ptu/backend/common/api/ApiErrorWriter.java` — single writer used by 401/403/429:
  ```java
  public final class ApiErrorWriter {
      private ApiErrorWriter() {}
      public static void write(ObjectMapper objectMapper, HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response,
              HttpStatus status, String message) throws IOException {
          response.setStatus(status.value());
          response.setContentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE);
          response.setCharacterEncoding("UTF-8");
          objectMapper.writeValue(response.getOutputStream(),
                  ApiError.of(status.value(), status.getReasonPhrase(), message, request));
      }
  }
  ```
- `backend/src/main/java/com/ptu/backend/common/security/RateLimiter.java` — `@Component`, fixed window, fail-open:
  ```java
  private static final String KEY_PREFIX = "rate_limit:";
  public RateLimitDecision acquire(String scope, String identity, AppProperties.Limit limit) {
      long windowSeconds = Math.max(limit.window().toSeconds(), 1);
      long now = System.currentTimeMillis() / 1000;
      long windowIndex = now / windowSeconds;
      long secondsLeft = windowSeconds - (now % windowSeconds);
      String key = KEY_PREFIX + scope + ":" + identity + ":" + windowIndex;
      try {
          Long count = redis.opsForValue().increment(key);
          if (count != null && count == 1L) redis.expire(key, Duration.ofSeconds(windowSeconds));
          if (count == null) return RateLimitDecision.permit();
          return count <= limit.requests() ? RateLimitDecision.permit() : RateLimitDecision.deny(secondsLeft);
      } catch (DataAccessException ex) {
          log.warn("Rate limiter is unavailable, allowing request: {}", ex.getMessage());
          return RateLimitDecision.permit();
      }
  }
  public record RateLimitDecision(boolean allowed, long retryAfterSeconds) {
      static RateLimitDecision permit() { return new RateLimitDecision(true, 0); }
      static RateLimitDecision deny(long retryAfterSeconds) { return new RateLimitDecision(false, retryAfterSeconds); }
  }
  ```
- `backend/src/main/java/com/ptu/backend/common/security/RateLimitFilter.java` — `OncePerRequestFilter` (not a bean; instantiated in `SecurityConfig` so Boot does not auto-register it as a servlet filter):
